# Stale reference 3 — storage-description prof:hasResource points at the
# meta/profiles/source PROF descriptor, which 404s. This is a SECOND-ORDER
# consequence of the same source->concept merge that pod_audit did NOT flag
# (the auditor only checks rdfs:seeAlso / catalog pointers, not the
# prof:hasResource profile set), found by manually walking the storage
# description during this curation pass.
<urn:uuid:919ef3f8-4908-4aec-9cd4-9c30c2a81e54>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/meta/profiles/concept> ;   # the surviving profile for concept/source content
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:DanglingReference ;
    mem:rationale "Storage description prof:hasResource lists <../meta/profiles/source>, which returns 404 — the per-kind PROF profile descriptor for the merged-away source kind. The sibling <../meta/profiles/concept> resolves 200 and is the profile for concept-class content; since sources are now concepts, the source profile entry is dangling and redundant. GUARD CHECK performed: <../meta/profiles/page> in the same prof:hasResource list also looked suspicious (pages renamed) but it resolves 200 and is the ROOT profile that concept/person/howto/working/place/event all profile from (rdfs:label 'Wiki-Memory L3 — Page profile') — it is current, NOT stale; left untouched. Only profiles/source is stale. Resolved against the live profile set. Repair direction: pointer -> reality. Lives in STATIC css/config/void-description.json -> repo edit." ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:16:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

